  "_commit": {
    "id": "769f4de98ff2535707b1a62ef3fad02600787007",
    "author": "Sehyun Oh <shbrief@gmail.com>",
    "committer": "Sehyun Oh <shbrief@gmail.com>",
    "message": "Migrate gcloud/gsutil calls to GCPtools for Bioc 3.23\n\nAnVILGCP 1.7.x removed the gcloud_* functions (fully migrated to\nGCPtools) and marked the gsutil_* functions defunct; gsutil_cp was\ndropped in favour of the avcopy generic. AnVIL no longer exports any\nof them. This caused 1 ERROR and 2 WARNINGs on the devel builder.\n\n* setCloudEnv(), cloneWorkspace(): call GCPtools::gcloud_exists(),\n  gcloud_account() and gcloud_project() explicitly. Qualifying rather\n  than importing avoids \"replacing previous import\" warnings on the\n  release branch, where AnVILGCP still exports the deprecated shims.\n* .biobakery_currentInput(): AnVIL::gsutil_cat() -> GCPtools::gsutil_cat().\n  AnVILGCP's copy is defunct and raises an error.\n* getOutput(): replace gsutil_cp with the avcopy generic.\n* .nonMetadataOutputs(): fix Rd cross-reference to avworkflow_files,\n  which lives in AnVILGCP rather than AnVIL.\n* getAllDataTables(): use the has_avworkspace() example guard used\n  elsewhere in the package; the previous guard called the now-removed\n  AnVILGCP::gcloud_exists().\n* Add R/globals.R declaring the NSE column names used by dplyr verbs\n  and the magrittr placeholder, clearing the \"no visible binding for\n  global variable\" NOTE.\n* DESCRIPTION: add GCPtools to Imports and rmarkdown to Suggests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n",
    "time": 1788173080
  },
